{"source":"github","project_id":"academydatasets","target":"rstudio/academyDatasets","id":"pr/32","ref":32,"title":"Use `vctrs` to generate column types in data dictionaries","description":"Use `vctrs::vec_ptype_abbr()` instead of `type()` in `describe_dataset()` to generate column types in data dictionaries and documentation. This solves an issue where non-base classes would be labelled with a misleading base type (e.g. `factor` as `integer`, date-time as `double`).\r\n\r\n`vctrs::vec_ptype_abbr()` is used in the print method of `tibble` columns, so the labels should be familiar and compact.\r\n\r\nCloses #29.","published_at":"2021-08-24T02:16:53Z","updated_at":"2021-08-24T17:31:10Z","url":"https://github.com/rstudio/academyDatasets/pull/32","tags":["documentation"],"type":"pr","extra":{"author":"rossellhayes","merged_at":"2021-08-24T17:31:10Z","state":"MERGED"}}
